# 🐧 Linux System Health Checker

## Project Description

This project is a Bash script designed to collect important information about a Linux Mint computer and perform basic system health checks.

The script checks:

* Hostname
* Current user
* Linux distribution
* Kernel version
* System uptime
* CPU information
* Memory usage
* Disk usage
* IP address
* Internet connectivity
* Available system updates

## Script

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "======================================"
echo "       LINUX SYSTEM HEALTH CHECK"
echo "======================================"

echo ""
echo "SYSTEM INFORMATION"
echo "--------------------------------------"

echo "Hostname: $(hostname)"
echo "User: $USER"
echo "Kernel: $(uname -r)"

if command -v lsb_release >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "Distribution: $(lsb_release -ds)"
fi

echo "Uptime: $(uptime -p)"

echo ""
echo "CPU INFORMATION"
echo "--------------------------------------"
echo "CPU: $(lscpu | grep 'Model name' | head -1 | cut -d ':' -f2 | xargs)"
echo "CPU Cores: $(nproc)"

echo ""
echo "MEMORY USAGE"
echo "--------------------------------------"
free -h

echo ""
echo "DISK USAGE"
echo "--------------------------------------"
df -h /

echo ""
echo "NETWORK INFORMATION"
echo "--------------------------------------"

IP_ADDRESS=$(hostname -I | awk '{print $1}')

echo "IP Address: $IP_ADDRESS"

echo ""
echo "INTERNET CONNECTIVITY"
echo "--------------------------------------"

if ping -c 1 -W 2 google.com > /dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "Internet: CONNECTED"
else
    echo "Internet: NOT CONNECTED"
fi

echo ""
echo "SYSTEM UPDATES"
echo "--------------------------------------"

sudo apt update -qq

UPDATES=$(apt list --upgradable 2>/dev/null | grep -c upgradable)

echo "Available Updates: $UPDATES"

echo ""
echo "======================================"
echo "          HEALTH CHECK COMPLETE"
echo "======================================"
```

## How to Run

Give the script permission to execute:

```bash
chmod +x system-health-check.sh
```

Run the script:

```bash
./system-health-check.sh
```

